  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133305/assets/38f113226c13332a07fdd6059819de5cf69147dbbfea3d1710325ef7776e5538.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of pentagons}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of pentagons. There are $4$ pentagons.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is $4:7.$",
